    "summary": "High‑energy 9/17/82 Portland show – Touch of Grey debut, monster Morning Dew & Spanish jam",
    "review": "The September 17, 1982 night at the Cumberland County Civic Center is one of the most electrifying late‑summer shows of the era.  The band bursts out with a smoking Bertha → Promised Land opener and rolls into a historic set that includes the first live rendition of Touch of Grey, a thunderous Spanish Jam that morphs into a Phil chant and a monster The Other One, and a soaring Morning Dew that rides over a blistering Throwing Stones → Deal transition.  Across every source – pristine soundboard, crystal‑clear matrix tapes and even the best audience captures – the energy stays sky‑high; Brent Mydland’s organ/piano adds a warm, country‑western flavor while Phil Lesh lays down “bass bombs” that drive the jams.  Garcia’s lead work is on fire from start to finish, delivering his signature solos on Dew and Deal, and the dual‑drum section keeps the momentum relentless.  In short, this show captures the band at a creative peak, with tight transitions, high‑octane improvisation, and a setlist that still feels fresh today.",
